@* The container of the edge bubbles (03 sections 3.4 and 4.6): empty on purpose. A member outside the visible rectangle is shown as a bubble on the edge of
   the map, and realmMap.js creates and moves those bubbles inside this element from the member payload, once per map frame, so C# is not involved per
   frame. The component exists so that the DOM order, and with it the focus order of 01 section 10.2, is explicit: the bubbles come after the map and its
   attribution control and before the sheet and the right stack. The group role gives the name a role to sit on; the element itself takes no pointer events
   (realm-map.css), so the map stays draggable under it. Blazor never diffs the children the script adds, because Razor renders none. *@
<div class="realm-bubbles" role="group" aria-label="Members off screen"></div>
